If you disagree with the contents of a page or want to make a change that you think will be contentious, rather than engaging in an editing war, it's preferable to talk about the change first and attempt to come to a consensus. UnanimousConsent is a good AnCap idea, eh?

JunkerIn proposed a convention for this. Create a new page named by "Talk" at the end of the discussed page's name. Put a link to the discussion page at the bottom of the discussed page and a back-link to the discussed page at the top of the discussion page. Example below.

